    "text": "Recent UAV-oriented benchmarks focus on scene understanding, event recognition, or navigation completion, but do not jointly assess the dual-cognition capability required for UAV agents.",
    "topic": "UAV benchmark limitations"
  },
  {
    "text": "UAV-DualCog is a benchmark for aerial multiview spatio-temporal reasoning that addresses the gap by evaluating both the UAV's own state and the external environment.",
    "topic": "UAV-DualCog benchmark"
  },
  {
    "text": "The benchmark is built on a dual-cognition perspective, emphasizing reasoning about both the UAV's state and the external environment in multiview spatio-temporal contexts.",
    "topic": "Dual-cognition perspective"
  },
  {
    "text": "Existing benchmarks typically do not jointly assess the UAV's self-awareness and spatial cognition in aerial scenarios.",
    "topic": "Self-awareness and spatial cognition"
  },
  {
    "text": "UAV-DualCog aims to evaluate the reasoning capabilities required for UAV agents to operate effectively in complex aerial environments.",
    "topic": "UAV reasoning capabilities"
  }
]
